  "term": "kick",
  "says": "Reid's synthesised bass drum: a sine whose pitch starts an octave or two up and drops to the drum's body (40-80 Hz) within a few tens of milliseconds - the pitch envelope is the beater's transient and gives the 'punch' - while the amplitude decays to silence in a few hundred milliseconds; a short click or noise burst at the very start for attack, and nothing sustained. Signature: an instant attack, a fundamental in the body region once the pitch has settled, a decay to -20 dB between 0.1 and 0.6 s, almost no energy above 1 kHz after the click, dead silent after.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Synth Secrets",
